lly. The company operates through two segments, Genie Retail Energy and Genie Renewables. It resells electricity and natural gas to residential and small business customers in the Eastern and Midwestern United States and Texas; and develops, constructs, and operates utility-scale solar energy projects. The company also distributes solar panels; offers energy procurement and advisory services to industrial, commercial, and municipal customers; and markets solar and alternative products and services. Genie Energy Ltd. was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Newark, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael M. Stein | Chief Executive Officer | Age 41 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 139 people. Revenue per employee of $3.6M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Genie Energy Ltd. is a small-cap utilities business with a $482M market cap on $502M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 31% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 24-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 41\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 26% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.26142428634874953},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Utilities peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Utilities peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Utilities \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Financial quality scores above most Utilities peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Genie Energy (NYSE:GNE) Sets New 1-Year High After Analyst Upgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/genie-energy-nysegne-sets-new-1-year-high-after-analyst-upgrade.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794433306.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"(GNE) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/GNE_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_111126021402_1794424442.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794424442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Genesis Energy (NZSE:GNE) Could Be 8% Below Fair Value Following Leadership Reshuffle","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/nz/utilities/nzx-gne/genesis-energy-shares/news/genesis-energy-nzsegne-could-be-8-below-fair-value-following","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794305857.726,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.965,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why You Might Be Interested In Genie Energy Ltd. (NYSE:GNE) For Its Upcoming Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-gne/genie-energy/news/why-you-might-be-interested-in-genie-energy-ltd-nysegne-for-1","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794142683.172,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"What Genie Energy (GNE) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/genie-energy-gne-said-q3-111705081.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794050225.0,"origin":"tiingo","se